/-!
## The point group of benzene

Benzene has molecular point group `D₆ₕ`, which is the direct product of the dihedral
group `D₆` (of order `12`, the symmetries of the hexagonal carbon skeleton in its own
plane) with the two element group `{E, i}` generated by the inversion centre.  Thus
`D₆ₕ ≅ D₆ × C₂` has order `24`.
-/

/-- The point group `D₆ₕ` of benzene, realised as `D₆ × C₂`. -/
abbrev D6h : Type := DihedralGroup 6 × Multiplicative (ZMod 2)

/-- The nontrivial element of the `C₂` factor, i.e. the inversion `i`. -/

def inv2 : Multiplicative (ZMod 2) := Multiplicative.ofAdd (1 : ZMod 2)

/-!
## The twelve conjugacy classes

Representatives of the twelve conjugacy classes of `D₆ₕ`, in the standard
chemists' ordering

`E, C₂, 2C₆, 2C₃, 3C₂', 3C₂''` (gerade part) and
`i, σ_h, 2S₃, 2S₆, 3σ_d, 3σ_v` (ungerade part),

each of the second six being the product of the corresponding element of the first
six with the inversion `i`.
-/
